Required attributions
---------------------

OpenStreetMap
  The travel time and distance matrices (problems/*/durations_s.csv.gz,
  problems/*/distances_m.csv.gz) and the location coordinates in
  problems/*/problem.json are derived from OpenStreetMap data.
  Map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open
  Database License: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  Routing: OSRM (Open Source Routing Machine).

Eurostat
  Customer locations were drawn in proportion to the population of the
  1 km cells of the Eurostat Census 2021 population grid (version 3).
  Source: Eurostat, Census 2021 population grid. (c) European Union.
  Data modified: cells near Budapest and Pecs, reduced to their centres
  and used as sampling weights; the grid itself is not included.
  Eurostat is not responsible for this dataset or for any use made of it.
  https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/help/copyright-notice

What the ODbL asks of you, in short (the licence text governs): if you
publicly use or share this database or a database derived from it, keep
these notices and the licence; a derived database you use publicly must
be offered under the ODbL (share-alike), together with a machine-readable
copy of it or of the changes. Works produced from the database (for
example a figure or a table of results) need an attribution notice, not
the share-alike licence.
